Actually, even better: I can reason it out myself and verify empirically. The design question: where should converters be applied?

Option A: in `SQLInsertCompiler.execute_sql` — apply `get_converters(self.returning_fields)` / `apply_converters` to the fetched rows (mirroring `results_iter`).

Option B: in `Model.save_base`/`bulk_create` — call `field.from_db_value` per value. Ugly, misses backend converters.

Option A is clearly the right, minimal, architecture-consistent fix: the compiler already has `get_converters`/`apply_converters` machinery used by `results_iter`; the insert path just never uses it.

